<title>UK: UK Labour condemn jobless &quot;fantasy figures&quot;.</title>
<headline>UK Labour condemn jobless &quot;fantasy figures&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stephen Byers, employment spokesman for Britain's main opposition Labour Party, condemned the latest fall in jobless figures for February as &quot;fantasy figures.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;What we do know is that one in five households, families have no one in work. Since John Major became Prime Minister, we have lost one million jobs. Those are the true figures and reflect what is happening in the real world,&quot; he told Sky News.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
